@startuml alert-lifecycle
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

state "FaultWatcher" as Watcher {
  state "Clear" as Clear
  state "Pending" as Pending : hold timer running
  state "Raised" as WatcherRaised

  [*] --> Clear
  Clear --> Pending : fault found,\nforSeconds > 0
  Clear --> WatcherRaised : fault found,\nno hold
  Pending --> Clear : fault gone
  Pending --> WatcherRaised : hold elapsed,\nfault still found
  WatcherRaised --> Clear : rule recovered
}

state "MonitoredAlert" as Alert {
  state "Idle" as Idle
  state "Raised" as AlertRaised : mitigations ran,\nescalation running
  state "Acknowledged" as Acknowledged : escalation stopped

  [*] --> Idle
  Idle --> AlertRaised : raiseFault()
  AlertRaised --> Acknowledged : Acknowledge button\nor dismissal
  AlertRaised --> Idle : clearFault()\nfollow-up "Cleared."
  Acknowledged --> Idle : clearFault()\nfollow-up "Cleared."
}

note right of Watcher
  Evaluated at start, on every reading change
  and every recheck interval of a RecheckedAlertRule.
  Changes made while the listener runs are
  evaluated once it returns.
end note

note right of Alert
  FaultWatcher entering Raised calls raiseFault();
  leaving Raised calls clearFault().
  stopMonitoring() returns to Idle from any state.
end note
@enduml
